WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:04.289
It shows you where the spelling gets stuck.

3
00:00:04.989 --> 00:00:10.966
You hold the grown-up page, turned away from your child. Your child gets the other page and a pencil.

4
00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:12.594
There are three parts.

5
00:00:13.044 --> 00:00:18.794
Part A. You say a word. Your child says its sounds, one by one, and touches a box for each.

6
00:00:19.244 --> 00:00:21.662
Show how once, with the word at. Like this.

7
00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:26.900
Mark a word if your child says every sound, in order.

8
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:34.024
Part B. Now you say one sound, and your child writes its letter. Say the short sound, not the name of the letter.

9
00:00:34.474 --> 00:00:37.648
These five are the ones to listen to before you start.

10
00:00:43.211 --> 00:00:49.982
Part C. You say a word once, and your child writes it. Mark it only if every letter is there, in the right order.

11
00:00:50.432 --> 00:00:54.104
Do not teach, and do not correct today. Just listen and mark.

12
00:00:54.554 --> 00:01:00.270
Then read the yellow box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

13
00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.511
That line tells you where the sticking point is: hearing the sounds, picking the letter, or keeping the order.

14
00:01:06.961 --> 00:01:11.639
Write the three numbers on the page, and keep it. You will look at it again on the last day.
